      "title": "Adjunct Instructor; Vertebrate Zoology BIOL322 - Spring Semester 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Adjunct Instructor; Vertebrate Zoology BIOL322 - Spring Semester 2027 Institution: Minnesota State University, Moorhead Classification Title: State Univ Adjunct Unit Bargaining Unit / Union: 209: Inter Faculty Organization City: Moorhead FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Part time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Limited Academic (Fixed Term) Salary Range: $0.00 - $0.00 Position Purpose: Support the mission of Minnesota State University Moorhead's School of Science by teaching biology courses to majors and nonmajors.  This teaching assignment includes both the lecture and laboratory components, totaling up to 6 credits. Responsibilities: Teach BIOL 322 and 322L; Vertebrate Zoology Lecture & Lab Effectively engage and communicate with students in the course Work with Learning Assistants to help students successfully complete labs and lab reports Salary Range : $1,888 per credit Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Biology, Environmental Sciences, Ecology, or related field. Prior undergraduate teaching experience in Biology Effective oral and written communication skills  Demonstrated commitment to fostering a supportive learning environment for undergraduate learners with diverse backgrounds and levels of previous experience and knowledge. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate degree in Biology or related field Evidence of successful teaching in Biology Other Requirements: The successful candidate must be able to lawfully accept employment in the United States by the day employment begins. The University regrets that we are unable to offer H1-B sponsorship at this time.  Official transcript(s) from all degree granting institutions must be provided to the Office of Human Resources prior to first duty day. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Inte